{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And he trembled.</b> As the Targum renders: וּתְוַהּ — a term of astonishment. Its midrash: he saw Gehenna opened beneath him." "<b>Who then.</b> מִי serves for oneself together with several words; אֵפֹה — אַיֵּה פֹּה: 'Who is he and where is he, the one who hunted game?'" "<b>And ate of all.</b> Of all the flavors I sought to taste, I tasted in it (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>He shall remain blessed.</b> Lest you say: had Jacob not deceived his father, he would not have taken the blessings — therefore he agreed and blessed him of his own will (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:48.866410004Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}